  "title": "The time-course of feature-based attention effects dissociated from temporal expectation and target-related processes",
  "description": "Human EEG recordings from 20 participants viewing rapid sequences of overlaid oriented grating pairs while detecting a target grating of a specific orientation. Feature-based attention was manipulated by cueing one of two gratings by colour, and temporal expectation was manipulated by making stimulus onset timing predictable or unpredictable. The dataset supports investigation of the time-course of attention effects dissociated from temporal expectation and target-related processes.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded from 20 participants during a session of about 1 hour. Participants viewed rapid sequences of overlaid oriented gratings, attended one colour-cued grating while ignoring the other, and detected a target orientation. Stimulus onset timing was either predictable or unpredictable.",
